note('Author page 12, archive 30. The page introduces the pole identifications and paths tilde-d, then expresses their images under u by tilde-beta = zeta sigma-infinity(zeta)^{-1}. The author explicitly queries rho versus rho^{-1} with a circled “rho^{-1} ?” above (39); both the original rho and the query are retained. In (41), the product uses plain d, although the defined pole-to-pole paths are tilde-d. Endpoint typing from (40) shows that the asserted inverse relation belongs to tilde-d; the unadorned product is not repaired. The norm-one identity (45) follows formally from (44) if sigma-infinity is involutive: zeta sigma(zeta)^{-1} sigma(zeta) zeta^{-1}=1. This conditional cancellation was checked, not a fresh proof of the involutivity assumption. The heavily overwritten operator in (43) remains sigma/tau uncertain. The short right marginal note is partly cancelled and only partly legible.')
check('031-41-endpoints','targeted proof check','From d_i^omega: P^omega→Q_i, the plain product d_i^omega d_i^{omega-prime} is not composable. The tilde-d definition in (40) gives mutually inverse pole-to-pole paths; preserve the written missing tildes.')
